ay-peat-forum-attract-the-craziest-people.438829/"},{"title":"Poliquin Bio-signature","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/poliquin-bio-signature/162025","site":"T Nation · 986 posts · 2011"},{"title":"2008 NBA Playoff Thread","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/2008-nba-playoff-thread/103912","site":"T Nation · 746 posts · 2008"},{"title":"Feel Better on Less Frequency/Higher One Time Dose?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/feel-better-on-less-frequency-higher-one-time-dose/274756","site":"T Nation · 267 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Where Do I Go From Here? Desperate Cry for Help","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/where-do-i-go-from-here-desperate-cry-for-help/251349","site":"T Nation · 242 posts · 2019"},{"title":"Low T Problem - Full Lab Info Provided","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/low-t-problem-full-lab-info-provided/161522","site":"T Nation · 141 posts · 2011"},{"title":"What Does Elevated Progesterone Mean in Men?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/what-does-elevated-progesterone-mean-in-men/262168","site":"T Nation · 138 posts · 2019"},{"title":"Election Results Summed Up","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/election-results-summed-up/204867","site":"T Nation · 81 posts · 2014"},{"title":"Caffeine Addicts Anonymous","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/caffeine-addicts-anonymous/193474","site":"T Nation · 77 posts · 2013"},{"title":"Butter and Mayo","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/butter-and-mayo/29573","site":"T Nation · 75 posts · 2003"},{"title":"Fish Oil and the Male Libido","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/fish-oil-and-the-male-libido/48783","site":"T Nation · 75 posts · 2005"},{"title":"How to 'Fix' Cortisol?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/how-to-fix-cortisol/119113","site":"T Nation · 43 posts · 2008"},{"title":"Age 69, Crazy Labs after Stopping TRT","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/age-69-crazy-labs-after-stopping-trt/277527","site":"T Nation · 41 posts · 2022"},{"title":"Adding Proviron to TRT (Post Finasteride Syndrome)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/adding-proviron-to-trt-post-finasteride-syndrome/247873","site":"T Nation · 37 posts · 2018"},{"title":"Protocol Suggestions / Bloodwork Interpretation","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/protocol-suggestions-bloodwork-interpretation/280080","site":"T Nation · 36 posts · 2022"},{"title":"CT's New Article: 6 Diet Facts That'll Blow Your Damn Mind","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/cts-new-article-6-diet-facts-thatll-blow-your-damn-mind/275601","site":"T Nation · 36 posts · 2021"}],"web":[]},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["The Ray Peat diet is an eating pattern inspired by the writings of Raymond Peat, an American author on nutrition and physiology. Followers describe it as \"pro-metabolic\" and aimed at correcting hormonal imbalances and raising metabolic rate. Typical elements are milk, cheese, fruit and fruit juice, root vegetables, eggs, shellfish, muscle and organ meats, collagen, and saturated fats such as butter and coconut oil, while polyunsaturated fats are avoided.[1]","On looksmax.org the diet is discussed alongside claims about hormones, thyroid function and even height. No clinical trials of the diet were found in the sources reviewed, and the wiki records community claims as claims."],"infobox":[["Type","Dietary pattern"],["Inspired by","Raymond Peat"],["Emphasises","Dairy, fruit and juice, root vegetables, eggs, shellfish[1]"],["Limits","Polyunsaturated fats (nuts, seeds, seed oils, fatty fish)[1]"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["As summarised in a looksmax.org post quoting a hospital dietitian, the diet emphasises healthy saturated fats, a heavy share of dairy, abundant fresh fruit and juice, root vegetables, animal protein and collagen. Followers cite the instability of PUFAs to explain why they are excluded.[1]","Community resource threads collect Peat's writings on metabolic rate and hormones, sodium and water retention, and nicotine.[2][3][4]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"In looksmaxxing communities","paras":["Forum members discuss the diet for hormones, skin and metabolism. One thread asserted that Peat gained roughly an inch in height in his 40s with DHEA supplementation; a reply expressed scepticism, noting that Peat made many other claims of rapid recovery.[5] Another thread pairs Peat's approach with raw animal-food diets.[6]","Community opinion is divided; thread titles include both enthusiastic and critical reactions."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"On looksmax.org the Ray Peat diet is treated as a metabolism and hormone optimisation approach, with competing views on its credibility.[1][5]","claims":[{"claim":"The diet raises metabolism and corrects hormonal imbalance","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Peat grew about an inch in his 40s using DHEA","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"RAY PEAT inspired post.","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ray-peat-inspired-post.2114091/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2023,"type":"forum"},{"title":"ray peat resource list resources to optimise metabolic rate hormones and health","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ray-peat-resource-list-resources-to-optimise-metabolic-rate-hormones-and-health.817948/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2022,"type":"forum"},{"title":"ray peat view on sodium and water retention","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ray-peat-view-on-sodium-and-water-retention.702760/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2022,"type":"forum"},{"title":"ray peat forum on nicotine studies attached","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ray-peat-forum-on-nicotine-studies-attached.632577/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2021,"type":"forum"},{"title":"Ray Peat gained at least an inch in his 40s with DHEA","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ray-peat-gained-at-least-an-inch-in-his-40s-with-dhea.1005348/","source":"looksmax.org","year":2021,"type":"forum"},{"title":"aajonus vonderplanitz x ray peat the ultimate bioenergetic primal vril stack","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/aajonus-vonderplanitz-x-ray-peat-the-ul